{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he asked Pharaoh's officers who were with him in the prison of his master's house</b> — It would have been fitting for Scripture to say, 'And he asked them, saying.' But it elaborated because it wished to tell in praise of Joseph, that he was a young slave, yet he asked two great officials — and in the house of his master who hated him — and each one of them had the power to order that his head be lifted from upon him, yet he did not fear them, but asked them and told them his opinion on the interpretation, for he trusted in his wisdom: for if the chief baker had escaped, he would have suspected him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:42:14.449906071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}